From: Juerg Haefliger <juerg.haefliger@canonical.com>

Add initial support for the HP EliteBook 6 G1q. This particular model is
based on the Qualcomm Snapdragon X1P42100 SoC and sports a touchscreen,
5MP IR camera, WCN785x Wifi/BT, fingerprint reader, Ethernet NIC and WWAN
modem.

The new dtsi is based on the existing x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi with:
- added declarations to support the additional base board components of
  the EliteBook, namely an integrated fingerprint reader, Ethernet NIC
  and HDMI-A port.
- removed touchscreen and Wifi declarations which are optional and belong
  in the model dts.

Working:
- Keyboard
- Touchpad
- Touchscreen
- USB A and C ports
- Ethernet NIC
- HDMI-A port
- Wifi
- Bluetooth
- Integrated Speakers and microphone
- Camera
- Fingerprint reader
- WWAN modem

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Juerg Haefliger <juerg.haefliger@canonical.com>
